      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Checked into this and the group resource is a NonRDFSource object. I'm guessing because the http client appends a charset to the content-type and then \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-3312\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3312\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Creating RDFSource with Content-type with charset results in a NonRDFSource\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-3312\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n takes over. I have tested the same behaviour in fcrepo4-tests without a charset in the content-type and it seems to work.</p>",
     "created": "27/May/20 9:49 PM",
